{"items":[{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-109411"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","first_seen_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-109411","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-10-28T19:17:45.459000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","https://attachments.samba.org/attachment.cgi?id=19294","https://attachments.samba.org/attachment.cgi?id=19295","https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-109411","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/109xxx/CVE-2026-109411.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-109411","https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2552136","https://bugzilla.samba.org/show_bug.cgi?id=16276","https://gitlab.com/samba-team/samba"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-109411"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-109411","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-109411"},"summary":"An access control bypass flaw was identified in Samba's vfs_ceph_rgw module in it's openat() function. An authenticated user can bypass access controls to read or overwrite restricted files on shares configured with the experimental vfs_ceph_rgw module. When a client requests an existing file using mismatched character casing, the module fails to perform a case-insensitive lookup correctly, causing the server to treat the operation as creating a new file. As a result, the server skips standard permission checks on the existing file, allowing the attacker to access or overwrite sensitive data owned by other users.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Samba: access control bypass via vfs_ceph_rgw case-insensitive open","topics":["advisory","cwe-178"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-10-30T02:46:07.844618Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-97229"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","first_seen_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-97229","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-10-13T01:05:46.166000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://docs.gitlab.com/releases/patches/patch-release-gitlab-19-4-2-released/","https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/work_items/630686","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/97xxx/CVE-2026-97229.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-97229","https://hackerone.com/reports/4055749","https://hackerone.com/reports/4058589","https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-97229"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-97229","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-97229"},"summary":"GitLab has remediated an issue in GitLab CE/EE affecting all versions from 19.2 before 19.2.8, 19.3 before 19.3.5, and 19.4 before 19.4.2 that, under certain conditions, could have allowed an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary code on the GitLab server via a specially crafted regular expression in a CI/CD configuration, due to insufficient regular expression validation.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Integer Overflow or Wraparound in GitLab","topics":["advisory","cwe-190"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-10-29T02:48:26.919957Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-92574"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","first_seen_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-92574","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-09-21T09:49:49.679000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-92574","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/92xxx/CVE-2026-92574.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-92574","https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2535436","https://github.com/cri-o/cri-o"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-92574"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-92574","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-92574"},"summary":"A vulnerability in CRI-O checkpoint restore allows a user who can create a pod from a malicious checkpointed container to bypass the destination Kubernetes security context. The restored process may retain credentials, Linux capabilities, no_new_privs, and seccomp state from the checkpoint instead of enforcing the destination configuration. This can allow execution with elevated privileges across the container security boundary.\nAffected upstream supported versions are CRI-O 1.34 and later. Downstream Red Hat products are affected from OCP 4.17 onward. Fixes have been applied to supported branches but are not yet released.\nExploitation requires permission to create a pod from a malicious checkpoint image and checkpoint restore functionality to be available.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Cri-o: cri-o checkpoint restore bypasses destination security context","topics":["advisory","cwe-250"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-10-28T02:30:44.695247Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-43961"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","first_seen_at":"2026-10-30T05:36:06.146065Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-43961","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-08-19T14:06:09.120000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/05/14/7","https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","https://catalog.redhat.com/software/containers/","https://github.com/vim/vim/","https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:57614","https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-43961","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/43xxx/CVE-2026-43961.json","https://github.com/vim/vim/security/advisories/GHSA-66hr-7p6x-x5j3","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-43961","https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2460434"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_sc